---
// Weapons 分类聚合页 —— CollectionPage schema（方案 3.1：列表页不标 Article）。
// 发售后：保留来源状态，已核实内容优先，避免把 Beta/前作信息误写成零售版事实。
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MediaFigure from '../../components/MediaFigure.astro';
import { SITE_IMAGES } from '../../data/images';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import PreReleaseNotice from '../../components/PreReleaseNotice.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import {
  WEAPONS,
  PREQUEL_ONLY_WEAPONS,
  WEAPON_CLASSIFICATION_NOTE,
  WEAPON_UPGRADE,
  UPGRADE_CAP_DISPUTE,
  WEAPONS_WITHOUT_ACHIEVEMENTS,
} from '../../data/weapons';

const title = 'Mortal Shell 2 Weapons — All 13 Weapons & Sidearms by Name';
const description =
  'All thirteen Mortal Shell 2 Weapons and Sidearms named from the retail achievement list, with unlock rates, patch-note buffs, and the disputed Tarforge upgrade cap.';

// 有 official 级机制事实的行数 —— 用来在正文里说明证据分布，不写死数字。
const patchedCount = WEAPONS.filter((w) => w.source.status === 'official' && w.knownStats.length > 1).length;

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Weapons', url: '/weapons/' },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schemaType="collection" breadcrumb={crumbs}>
  <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />

  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ash-100 md:text-4xl">Mortal Shell 2 Weapons Guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ash-400">
      Thirteen Weapons and Sidearms are named in the retail Steam achievement list, and the table is
      sorted by global unlock rate — the closest published proxy for the order players actually find
      them. Two post-launch patches name seven of the thirteen with balance changes, which is the first
      official mechanical detail for any of them. Upgrades reportedly cap at <strong>{WEAPON_UPGRADE.maxLevel} at the {WEAPON_UPGRADE.forge}</strong>,
      though several players report pushing past that with a late-game item; location maps are sold by
      <strong>{WEAPON_UPGRADE.mapMerchant}</strong>. Damage values, movesets and drop coordinates are
      published by nobody, so they are absent here rather than invented.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="mb-6"><PreReleaseNotice /></div>
  <section class="surface-card mb-8 border-amber-glow/20 bg-amber-glow/[0.04] p-5">
    <p class="section-kicker">Launch evidence</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">
      <a href="/mortal-shell-2-achievements/" class="hover:text-amber-glow">
        All 53 Mortal Shell 2 achievements and what they confirm
      </a>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash-400">
      The source for every name below, plus the eight
      <a href="/shells/" class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">Shell names</a>, the six collectible
      sets, and the Tarforge upgrade cap. For the Beta-era record of the Axe-and-Dagger objective,
      see the <a href="/mortal-shell-ii-open-beta-weapons-guide/" class="text-amber-glow hover:underline">Open Beta weapons guide</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <MediaFigure
      src={SITE_IMAGES.weaponsCloseup.src}
      alt={SITE_IMAGES.weaponsCloseup.alt}
      width={SITE_IMAGES.weaponsCloseup.width}
      height={SITE_IMAGES.weaponsCloseup.height}
      credit={SITE_IMAGES.weaponsCloseup.credit}
    />
  </div>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto surface-card">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-ash-900 text-left text-ash-300">
        <tr>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Weapon</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Unlock achievement</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Global unlock</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Category</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Known notes</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Status</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          WEAPONS.map((w) => (
            <tr class="border-t border-white/5 align-top hover:bg-ash-900/50">
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                <div class="font-medium text-ash-100">{w.name}</div>
                <div class="mt-1 text-ash-400">{w.summary}</div>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-300">{w.unlockAchievement ?? '—'}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 tabular-nums text-ash-300">
                {typeof w.unlockRate === 'number' ? `${w.unlockRate}%` : '—'}
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-400">{w.type}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-ash-300">
                <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
                  {w.knownStats.map((s) => (
                    <li>{s}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3"><StatusBadge status={w.source.status} /></td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <section class="prose-body mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-ash-300">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">What the post-launch patches confirmed</h2>
    <p>
      Cold Symmetry released two balance patches in the nine days after launch, and both named weapons
      individually with exact changes. <strong>{patchedCount} of {WEAPONS.length} rows</strong> now have official
      mechanical facts rather than only a name: the Great Martyr's Blade received (or was supposed to receive)
      an attack damage buff; the Axatana's weapon ability grants invulnerability frames and inflicts Fragile
      stacks; the Caged Hystrix and Triarch Repeater both fire and no longer require minimum resolve to do so;
      the Obsidian Hammer "now hits substantially harder" after a full balance pass; and the Salvaged Trebuchaxe's
      Tarred Fragment component was rebuilt because it was "simultaneously overpowered and broken". Those facts
      are drawn from developer posts, not player impressions, and they settle two things: <strong>Black Needle
      is a weapon</strong> (Balance Patch 1 lists it under "Weapons" with a light-attack improvement), and
      <strong>{WEAPON_UPGRADE.smeltCostReduction}</strong> (also Balance Patch 1).
    </p>
    <p>
      The six rows without patch mentions — Axe and Dagger, Forgotten Crossbow, Veteran's Battle Axe,
      Cursed Child, and Ballistazooka — still have only their names and unlock rates. No stats, no abilities.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">Why no row says "Weapon" or "Sidearm"</h2>
    <p>{WEAPON_CLASSIFICATION_NOTE}</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">The Tarforge upgrade cap: +16 or higher?</h2>
    <p>
      {UPGRADE_CAP_DISPUTE.guideClaim} That is the figure this page stated yesterday and the one most
      guides still cite. But at least four players report going higher — as high as +25 — after finding
      a forge upgrade item in a late-game chest. The reports:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
      {UPGRADE_CAP_DISPUTE.contradictingReports.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>
      {UPGRADE_CAP_DISPUTE.unresolved} The +16 figure is confirmed by the achievement at that level, but
      the higher numbers are grounded in posted builds and consistent across four independent reports. This
      is a live disagreement rather than a settled fact.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">Four weapons with no unlock achievement</h2>
    <p>
      The thirteen names above are the ones Valve tracks with unlock achievements, but they are not the
      full weapon list. Four more names appear in the corpus — three of them named in the official patches —
      with no "Unlock X" achievement at all:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
      {WEAPONS_WITHOUT_ACHIEVEMENTS.map((w) => <li><strong>{w.name}</strong>: {w.note}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>
      The Troubador's Lute is the remarkable one: Cold Symmetry gave it the largest single buff in Balance
      Patch 1 — Attack Damage +100% — yet it has no achievement. That means the thirteen-weapon count from
      Valve's achievement list is incomplete, and "Lord of War" (unlock all Weapons) does not in fact mean
      <em>all</em> weapons.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">Reading the unlock rates</h2>
    <p>
      Axe and Dagger (64.7%) and the Forgotten Crossbow (63.9%) are effectively tied, and both sit
      well above the 17.3% who finished the game — meaning they are found long before the end and are
      hard to miss. The Ballistazooka at 31.9% is the rarest, but note that the floor across all
      thirteen is fairly high: nothing here is at collectible-hunt rarity. That is consistent with
      "Lord of War" (unlock all Weapons) at 26.1% and "Guns. Lots of Guns" (unlock all Sidearms) at
      23.8% — roughly a quarter of players completed each set.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ash-500">
      Percentages are a snapshot read on 1 September 2026, twelve days after release, and they rise
      as more accounts play. Ordering by rate is an inference about where players find things, not a
      published route.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ash-100">Prequel weapons that did not return</h2>
    <p>
      {PREQUEL_ONLY_WEAPONS.join(', ')} were weapons in Mortal Shell (2020) and none of them appears
      in the retail achievement list. The thirteen names above account for the complete set, so earlier
      drafts of this page — which listed the prequel arsenal as probable sequel content — have been
      retired. The two genuine carry-overs are the <strong>Axatana</strong> (the first game's
      "Martelli Axatana") and <strong>Great Martyr's Blade</strong>, and even there the achievement
      list confirms only the name, not that the moveset is unchanged.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
